{#- A friendlier landing page for the footer's RSS link than the raw XML.
    Feed readers still find /feed.xml on their own through the
    <link rel="alternate"> in every page's <head>. #}
{%- set feedUrl = site.url + "/feed.xml" %}
<p>RSS had a hot minute and is less of a thing these days, but it should be!</p>

<p>Use an RSS reader like <a href="https://feedly.com/i/subscription/feed/{{ feedUrl | urlencode }}">Feedly</a> or <a href="https://www.inoreader.com/?add_feed={{ feedUrl | urlencode }}">Inoreader</a> to follow along with my site (and others) with no algorithm getting in the way. Everything I'm making, writing and notes will come through here. Give it a go!

<p>Paste this into your feed reader:</p>
<p class="rss-copy">
  <input type="text" readonly value="{{ feedUrl }}" aria-label="Feed address" onclick="this.select()">
  <button type="button" hidden>Copy</button>
</p>

<p>Or you can subscribe to my newsletter to get the odd update straight to your email inbox.</p>


<script>
  // the copy button only appears where the browser can copy
  (function () {
    var btn = document.querySelector(".rss-copy button");
    var input = document.querySelector(".rss-copy input");
    if (!navigator.clipboard) return;
    btn.hidden = false;
    btn.addEventListener("click", function () {
      navigator.clipboard.writeText(input.value).then(function () {
        btn.textContent = "Copied";
        setTimeout(function () { btn.textContent = "Copy"; }, 2000);
      });
    });
  })();
</script>
